#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# padded_form

#% text
# `padded_form(x, n)` shows the number `x` padded with spaces on the left to `n` characters; `padded_form(x, [n, f])` with `f` digits after the decimal point.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The argument is evaluated first; `padded_form` stays around the value as a display wrapper. The wrapper stays around the value: it is a display directive and changes no computation.

#% item
# Padding makes columns of numbers line up.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
padded_form(12.345, 8)
#% output
#= padded_form(12.345, 8)

#% cell
padded_form(12.345, [8, 2])
#% output
#= padded_form(12.345, [8, 2])

#% cell
padded_form([1.5, 22.25, 333.125], [8, 1])
#% output
#= padded_form([1.5, 22.25, 333.125], [8, 1])

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `number_form`, `decimal_form`, `string_pad`
